INT. COUNTY GENERAL - TRAUMA BAY ONE - NIGHT

Empty beds, drawn curtains, every monitor lit and waiting. A wall phone buzzes once. Hallway lights flicker.

DR. FELIX AMADI, forties, snaps a gown over his scrubs. DR. RENATA LINDQVIST, fifties, lines up chest tubes on a tray, in order, like silverware.

                    FELIX
          Bus rollover. Twenty-three patients, ETA four minutes.

                    RENATA
          Twenty-three. And we have six beds.

She doesn't stop working. He tears open a pack of gauze.

                    FELIX
          (to the room)
          Everyone in this bay, listen. Triage at the door. Red tags left, yellow center, green to the cafeteria.

                    RENATA
          (muttering)
          Green to the cafeteria. We should open a restaurant.

                    FELIX
          Renata, I need you at the door.

                    RENATA
          I need you to stop calling it "the door."

                    FELIX
          It's a door!

                    RENATA
          It's a funnel.

The wall phone buzzes again, urgently. They both reach for it, pull back, and speak at once.

                    FELIX
          Pick it up.

                    RENATA
          ^Don't pick it up.

The buzzing continues. They look at the phone, then at each other, then at the empty beds. Renata answers it with a sharp snap of her wrist.

                    RENATA (CONT'D)
          Trauma One. Go.

She listens. Her jaw tightens. She holds the receiver out to Felix without a word.
